{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121775","id":4134111334,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc72aYhm","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121775","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121775.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121775.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121775","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121775/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121775/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121775/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6f7e7a5200ffc59693a70fa356fdfd4b6cc63925","number":121775,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix directional shadow culling for orthogonal cameras","user":{"login":"benioriginal","id":111044589,"node_id":"U_kgDOBp5n7Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111044589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal","html_url":"https://github.com/benioriginal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benioriginal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\r\n\r\n### What does this fix?\r\n\r\nThis fixes incorrect directional shadow caster culling with orthogonal cameras.\r\n\r\nBefore\r\n<img width=\"1906\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-26 001954\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/565fa00c-157c-47ff-83b6-e60f05d8083f\" />\r\n\r\nAfter\r\n<img width=\"1917\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-26 001851\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd419f2b-6f67-4581-b672-49d87de4b044\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is a regression from the tighter per-cascade shadow caster culling introduced in #114678, it fixes incorrect directional shadow caster culling with orthogonal cameras, the issue being caused by the renderer and the light culler reconstruicting cascade bounds independently. The culler could then use different split distances and side planes from the cascade actually rendered, causing valid shadow casters to be removed.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### What changed?\r\n\r\nThe light culler now uses the actual cascade geometry directly, before it would internally recalculate these bounds, each cascade now passes its precise projected planes (and endpoints) to the light culler.\r\n\r\nThe existing directional silhouette and extrusion algorithm then constructs the tight caster volume from the cascade geometry data provided by each cascade. The directional culling behavior remains the same, and each cascade still defines its own set of culling planes.\r\n\r\nThe existing per-cascade tight culling optimization (#114678) is still active. I removed the redundant cascade volume reconstruction in the culler and its obsolete split state variable, shouldnt cause any issues , I mean everyone says that and then an issue appears lol, but no, im confident.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121644","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archi